cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Algorithmic Fairness in Machine Learning: A Multi-Dataset Analysis"
abstract: >
  An IEEE-style research investigation into demographic bias across four
  real-world ML classification tasks (Adult Census, COMPAS, Bank Marketing,
  Credit Default). Evaluates four classifiers under both standard performance
  metrics and three fairness operationalisations: demographic parity difference,
  equalised odds difference, and disparate impact ratio.
authors:
  - name: "NCI Dublin MSc Artificial Intelligence Group"
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshuajthomas/algorithmic-fairness-ml"
license: MIT
date-released: "2025-01-01"
keywords:
  - algorithmic fairness
  - machine learning
  - bias detection
  - disparate impact
  - demographic parity
  - equalised odds
  - COMPAS
  - adult census
  - credit default
  - bank marketing
